  "name": "Sine Space: The Eternal Return",
  "title": "Walking Through Sine",
  "lookup_name": "WaveFunctions_Sine_Space",
  "description": "What kinds of passage can a repeating rule make. In the antechamber a corridor of two facing sine walls runs east-west, 8 m long and 2 m wide, entered from its west mouth and leaving at its east mouth onto the head of the bridge. A panel at the entrance holds two sliders, AMP (both walls' amplitude) and PHASE (the offset between them), and two buttons, FREEZE and RESET; a readout prints the values in force and the narrowest and widest gap they make. The walls are visible surfaces only: they do not collide, and the passage that supports a body is the museum deck. The basin below the bridge keeps the sine_space floor, its colour balls and the dark sphere as the developed secondary arena. Structure recovered 2026-09-10: interior 2 = platform, perimeter w, wall_height 3.",
